project: dynamic memory manager utilizing a circular 1 way linked list

---------tradeoffs for implementation-----------

  - 1 way linked list advantages
      -simpler structure which reduces the memory overhead of the list.
      - can efficiently traverse the list by simply incrementing the Rover
      - better accuracy to user's requested memory as unit size smaller

  - 1 way linked list disadvantages
      - restricts movement to a single direction so can increase search time
        to find a target node

  - 2 way linked list advantages
      - would have allowed for easier access of previous nodes and faster search time
        for target nodes.
      - easier to preserve the chain when inserting or deleting a node from the list
  - 2 way linked list disadvantages
      - additional memory overhead.
      - worse accuracy to user's requested memory as unit size is larger



  - First fit advantages
      - better allocation speed as selects first block that is large enough

  - First fit disadvantages
      - has higher overall fragmentation rate than best fit

  - Best fit advantages
      - maximizes the usage of requested memory and is more memory efficient
      - lower fragmentation rate as will attempt to use up any block it can

  - Best fit disadvantages
      - lower allocation speed due to needing to search until exact match is
        found or entire list is traversed



  - effect of Coalessing
      - minimizes fragmentation by combining freed blocks when able
      - adds runtime to each alloc (I use free to place remaining block in sorted) 
        and free.
      - lowers memory overhead by reducing number of "active" headers in list

