As expected, system malloc and free are substancially faster than my versions.
Interestingly, adding flags significantly improved my code's response time.
I was unable to identify the exact cause, as both best fit and first fit
are done in the same loop, just with different conditions enabled. My theory
is that since equilibrium driver by default works with smaller sizes, best fit
was able to routinely completely remove nodes from the list and coalessing was able to
do the same for the free side of the operations.

