These additional tests reveal that coalessing is lowering the average runtime of my code when
compared to coalessing disabled. This is likely due the speed of reinserting nodes into the list
when it is already sorted. Also, these values are much closer to the system's functions times which
suggests that my algorithms are operating at a higher complexity class than the system's.


